# How to cite this repository. GitHub reads this file to render a
# "Cite this repository" button.
#
# There is no paper yet and no ledger claim is proved, so this cites the
# software and its definitions — not a result. When a result lands, add a
# `preferred-citation:` block naming the paper and leave this block in place
# for the development itself.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the definitions, the certificates or the ledger from this
  repository, please cite it as below.
title: "Superko Complexity"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked formalization of generalized Go under the positional and
  situational superko rules, with a ledger of complexity-theoretic claims and
  their evidence. The complexity classification of superko Go is open; this
  repository states the problem formally and records what is proved, what is
  cited, and what remains conjecture.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Piché"
    given-names: "Joseph J."
    email: "j@jpiche.com"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jpiche/superko-complexity"
keywords:
  - Go
  - superko
  - computational complexity
  - Lean 4
  - formalization
  - combinatorial game theory
